    "q-7027": {
      "dom_id": "step-q7027",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "The domain of the function $f(x)$ is $x\\ge 4$ and the range of $f$ is $f(x)\\ge 2.$ What is the range of the inverse function ${f}^{-1}(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall the following:\n\n- The domain of a function $f(x)$ is the range of its inverse function ${f}^{-1}(x).$\n\n- The range of a function $f(x)$ is the domain of its inverse function ${f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nThe domain of $f(x)$ is:\n\n$$\nx\\ge 4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)\\ge 4\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
