    "q-108477": {
      "dom_id": "step-q108477",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The domain of the function $f(x)$ is $-1\\le x\\le 9$ and the range of $f$ is $-2\\le f(x)\\le 11.$ What is the domain of the inverse function ${f}^{-1}(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall the following:\n\n- The domain of a function $f(x)$ is the range of its inverse function ${f}^{-1}(x).$\n\n- The range of a function $f(x)$ is the domain of its inverse function ${f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nThe range of $f(x)$ is:\n\n$$\n-2\\le f(x)\\le 11\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is:\n\n$$\n-2\\le x\\le 11\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
